---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getCatalog } from '../lib/catalog.js';

const { stats, revision } = await getCatalog();
const fmt = (n) => n.toLocaleString('en-US');
const built = new Date().toUTCString();
---

<Base title="About">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1 class="page-title">About this mirror</h1>

    <p>
      This site is a read-only mirror of
      <a href="https://keycap-archivist.com">Keycap Archivist</a>, the community
      archive of artisan keycaps. All catalog data comes from the
      <a href="https://github.com/keycap-archivist/database">keycap-archivist/database</a>
      project, which the community regenerates daily from each maker&rsquo;s own
      Google&nbsp;Doc catalog. Full credit for the data, the images, and years of
      archiving work belongs to the Keycap Archivist maintainers and the makers
      themselves.
    </p>

    <p>
      The mirror exists to keep the catalog browsable with as few moving parts
      as possible. It is a fully static site, rebuilt daily from the latest
      database revision: no accounts, no wishlists, no servers to break.
    </p>

    <h2>Catalog revision</h2>
    <dl class="rev">
      <dt>Makers</dt><dd>{fmt(stats.makers)}</dd>
      <dt>Sculpts</dt><dd>{fmt(stats.sculpts)}</dd>
      <dt>Colorways</dt><dd>{fmt(stats.colorways)}</dd>
      <dt>Database revision</dt>
      <dd>
        <a href={`https://github.com/keycap-archivist/database/commit/${revision.revision}`}>
          <code>{revision.revision.slice(0, 8)}</code>
        </a>
      </dd>
      <dt>Site built</dt><dd>{built}</dd>
    </dl>

    <h2>For makers</h2>
    <p>
      Want your catalog added or corrected? The data is maintained upstream:
      open an issue or pull request on
      <a href="https://github.com/keycap-archivist/database">keycap-archivist/database</a>
      (catalog templates are in the <code>templates/</code> folder there), and the
      change will appear here after the next daily sync.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .rev {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
    gap: 5px 20px;
  }
  .rev dt {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.625rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    align-self: baseline;
    padding-top: 3px;
  }
  .rev dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }
</style>
